Can you explain terraform lifecylce ?

Terraform Lifecycle" refers to two distinct related concepts
1.The Core Workflow Lifecycle
[Write] ➔ [Init] ➔ [Plan] ➔ [Apply] ➔ [State Management] ➔ [Destroy]
Write:--->we can write our .tf files according our requirements
Initialize (terraform init)----->Prepares the directory by downloading the necessary cloud provider plugins (like AWS, Azure, or GCP) and setting up our state backend.
Plan (terraform plan): ----->Compares our code against the current reality of our cloud environment. It prints a preview showing exactly what will be added, changed, or deleted.
Apply (terraform apply):----> Executes the changes outlined in the plan. It calls the cloud provider APIs to spin up or modify our physical resources
State Management: ---->Terraform updates a file (terraform.tfstate) that serves as a single source of truth, mapping our code definitions to the actual IDs of real-world resources
Destroy (terraform destroy): ----->Cleans up our infrastructure by safely deleting all 
resources tracked by that state file

2. The lifecycle Configuration Block

when we update an attribute that forces a resource to be recreated, Terraform deletes the old resource first and then creates the new one.To override this default behavior, we can insert a nested lifecycle block inside any resource configuration
create_before_destroy = true---->Forces Terraform to stand up a new replacement resource before tearing down the old one.
prevent_destroy = true--->Rejects any terraform apply or destroy command that attempts to delete this resource.
ignore_changes = [attr]------>Tells Terraform to look away if specific attributes change outside of the code---->Resources modified by external tools (e.g., cloud auto-scaling groups modifying instance counts or replica tags).
Example:
resource "aws_instance" "web_server" {
  ami           = "ami-123456"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
  lifecycle {
    create_before_destroy = true
    prevent_destroy       = false
  }
}
